  "title": "Route every gate run through gate.run_gate; timeout holds as gate_timeout infra failure (v2, test seams migrated)",
  "spec": "What: wire the bounded runner from T-1392 (orchestrator/gate.py, merged on goal/T-1391: settings, run_bounded, run_gate, running_gates) into every gate invocation, and make a final timeout an infrastructure failure instead of gate_red. Replaces T-1393 (held: spec review request_changes); its six findings are resolved below.\nWhy: a hung tests-green (luna xcodebuild 6 h) stalled goals, and killing it by hand marked the task gate_red, so the daemon filed a pointless code fix round.\n\nImport rule: daemon.py, merge.py and failures.py do `from orchestrator import gate` (module import, so tests can patch `daemon.gate.run_gate`, `merge.gate.run_gate`, `failures.gate.run_bounded`). gate.py must not import daemon, merge or failures.\n\nChanges:\n1. daemon.gate (daemon.py:1448): replace `subprocess.run([str(merge.TESTS_GREEN), worktree], ...)` with `result = gate.run_gate(worktree, script=merge.TESTS_GREEN, task_id=t[\"id\"], cfg=pool.cfg)`. Order after the call: first the existing `_hold_stale_high(t)` check (unchanged, still runs on a timeout: finding 5), then `if result[\"timed_out\"]:` stamp(t[\"id\"], \"gated_at\", pipeline_fields={\"infra_failure\": \"gate_timeout\", \"gate_timeouts\": pipeline.get(\"gate_timeouts\", 0) + result[\"timeouts\"]}, status=\"held\", hold_reason=\"gate_timeout\", resume_hint={\"gate_timeout_s\": gate.settings(pool.cfg)[\"timeout_s\"], \"output_tail\": (result[\"stdout\"] + result[\"stderr\"])[-4000:]}), notify(f\"{t['id']}: gate timed out twice; held as infra failure\"), continue. gate_reds is NOT incremented on a timeout. Then the existing red branch using result[\"returncode\"] and result[\"stderr\"], and the green path, unchanged.\n2. merge.merge (merge.py:57): replace the subprocess.run with `result = gate.run_gate(wt, script=TESTS_GREEN, task_id=task_id)` (cfg omitted: gate.settings(None) reads pool.config(); no signature change to merge.merge, finding 6). If result[\"timed_out\"]: bus.update(task_id, status=\"held\", hold_reason=\"gate_timeout\", pipeline={**(task.get(\"pipeline\") or {}), \"infra_failure\": \"gate_timeout\"}, resume_hint={\"output_tail\": (result[\"stdout\"]+result[\"stderr\"])[-4000:]}) and return {\"status\": \"gate_timeout\", \"reason\": \"gate_timeout\"}; the target branch must not move. Red stays status failed / tests_red exactly as today, using result[\"returncode\"] and result[\"stderr\"]. Keep `merge.TESTS_GREEN` as the module attribute tests patch.\n3. Flaky rerun (failures.failure_kind, failures.py:152): replace `subprocess.run(command, cwd=worktree, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=rerun_timeout)` with `rerun = gate.run_bounded(command, cwd=worktree, timeout_s=rerun_timeout)`. If rerun[\"timed_out\"]: append {\"ids\": ids, \"timed_out\": True, \"timeout_s\": rerun_timeout, \"output\": (rerun[\"stdout\"] + rerun[\"stderr\"])[-2000:]} and classify \"code_defect\", exactly the shape today's TimeoutExpired branch produces. Otherwise use rerun[\"returncode\"], rerun[\"stdout\"], rerun[\"stderr\"] where the CompletedProcess fields were used. The runner probe (failures.py:106, subprocess.run with timeout 60) stays as it is. daemon.auto_fix_round (daemon.py:171) passes rerun_timeout=min(flaky_rerun_timeout_s, gate.settings(pool.cfg)[\"timeout_s\"]).\n4. daemon.auto_fix_round (daemon.py:149): skip a held task whose hold_reason is \"gate_timeout\" or whose pipeline.infra_failure is set, before failure_kind runs: no fix round, no rerun, no probe.\n5. planner_runs.build_ctx (planner_runs.py:1021-1026): AFTER the cooling-source loop that may reassign `infra` (the `for source in [...]` block), add: `pipeline_infra = (task.get(\"pipeline\") or {}).get(\"infra_failure\"); if pipeline_infra: infra = pipeline_infra`. So a gate_timeout hold yields ctx[\"infra_failure_kind\"] == \"gate_timeout\" even when an account is also cooling (finding 4), and decision.route (decision.py:89) returns route \"none\". Do not change decision.py.\n\nTest migration (findings 1-3; these files are in scope, keep every existing test's intent):\n6. tests/test_daemon.py gate_green helper (line 1538): keep the subprocess.run fake for osascript and git passthrough, drop its TESTS_GREEN branch, and additionally `self.swap(daemon.gate, \"run_gate\", fake_gate)` where fake_gate(worktree, *, script, task_id=None, cfg=None) returns {\"returncode\": 0 if green else 1, \"stdout\": \"\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"timed_out\": False, \"attempts\": 1, \"timeouts\": 0}. The direct sites that match argv on [str(merge.TESTS_GREEN)] (around lines 3135, 3145, 3171, 3207, 3228, 3305) migrate the same way: patch daemon.gate.run_gate, record (worktree, script, task_id) per call, and assert on those instead of argv (e.g. line 3145 becomes assertEqual(gate_calls, [(str(self.sandbox), merge.TESTS_GREEN, tid)]); line 3171 asserts no gate call; 3207 asserts one).\n7. tests/test_daemon.py test_flaky_rerun_has_timeout_and_timeout_is_not_flaky (line 1907): keep the subprocess.run swap for the probe (return FakeProc(\"\", 1) for the `-c import pytest` argv; any other argv fails the test), and swap failures.gate.run_bounded with a fake that asserts timeout_s == 17 and returns {\"returncode\": None, \"stdout\": \"hung test\", \"stderr\": \"\", \"timed_out\": True, \"duration_s\": 17.0}. The assertions on failure_kind code_defect and flaky_runs [{\"ids\": [...], \"timed_out\": True, \"timeout_s\": 17, \"output\": \"hung test\"}] stay. test_runner_probe_timeout_does_not_block_or_mark_flaky (line 1767) is unchanged (the probe still uses subprocess.run).\n8. tests/test_merge.py lines 320-331: patch merge.gate.run_gate instead of orchestrator.merge.subprocess.run; assert it was called once with (str(wt)) positional and script=merge.TESTS_GREEN. Other test_merge tests that patch merge.TESTS_GREEN to a real script path keep working because gate.run_gate executes `script` (do not fake them).\n\nNew tests in tests/test_gate_timeout.py (created by T-1392; keep its tests): patch daemon.gate.run_gate / merge.TESTS_GREEN with a real sleeping script and a tiny [gate] timeout_s in the cfg, per the acceptance list. Never treat a timeout as success anywhere. Grep first for exact current names and line numbers; they may have shifted.",
